#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:5
#: fd1513a9c9224ae5ba73101ef7587351
msgid "Common Issues and Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:7
#: cb5ac8717f3143908eb24bb3719be5e0
msgid "This page details some of the most common issues with Balance Bots and possible solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:10
#: c2de066506da4999b41572a4250d0784
msgid "1) Manual/Hold Mode issues:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:13
#: 91aaa85f266b4e51887589bcee84651a
msgid "The vehicle struggles to balance or wobbles too much"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:15
#: bace128980144457bdc96a8ddcd456e0
msgid "**1) Motor Backlash** : The balancing depends on very fine adjustments of the wheel. So any backlash between gears of the motor could lead to poor balancing performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:18
#: c918166bbff24726beece040d4c71a0d
msgid "This is bad:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:23
#: 878b60eb069d4e45991c95b4c5f2acba
msgid "The only fix is to change motors. Make sure the backlash is as low as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:25
#: a0658005f0414692aa2fa3b328859990
msgid "**2) Weight Distribution** : If the center of gravity is near the wheels, the vehicle can topple quickly and if the motors are not fast enough to compensate, then the vehicle can become wobbly. The higher the center of gravity, the slower the vehicle falls. But more torque would be required from the motors to keep it balanced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:28
#: 10c0cbb9b1d84e81b992ded8bab8da1d
msgid "A good way to change the weight distribution is to move up/down the position of the batteries. How high depends on the torque and speed of the motors. In case of very fast motors with low torque, keep it closer to the wheels. If instead the motors are slow, but can provide high torque, then shift the center of mass higher by placing the batteries higher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:31
#: c436607a1a244f14a067fd1b37cfb959
msgid "**3) Minimum Throttle** : If the minimum throttle sent to the motors from the autopilot is **too low** to turn on the motors, then the Balance Bot will move back and forth struggling to keep balance. Sometimes this issue can also cause it to drift off in one direction and topple. If the minimum throttle value is **too high** then the Balance Bot will be able maintain balance, but will be very wobbly. Refer to this guide to set the :ref:`minimum throttle <balance_bot-configure-throttle>` value correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:34
#: e05ad14145664447a2f8739da9ccf5bd
msgid "**4) PID tuning** : Improper PID tuning, especially high P or I gains can cause the vehicle to become wobbly. An insufficient D gain can also make the vehicle wobbly, but a very high D gain can cause very fast wobbling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:39
#: 0cbeb1bbd8674195b49d7dbafb107eb9
msgid "The vehicle drifts off in one direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:41
#: df2a6168414547c69ee179fe42927036
msgid "**1) Accelerometer Calibration** : This can happen because the accelerometer calibration is invalid. Disturbing the autopilot, changing connections, crashes etc can disturb the acceleromter calibration. Do the accelerometer calibration again. Often, a one axis acccelerometer trim can fix this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-issues.rst:44
#: 013e7b3f0c2f46c6a4546bc7409d83a9
msgid "**2) Pitch trim** : The center of mass of the vehicle be slightly displaced from the zero pitch position. Hence the vehicle is not in equilibrium at 0 degrees pitch. This can be offset by :ref:`setting the pitch trim <balance_bot-tuning-pitch-trim>` parameter."
msgstr ""

